  "description": "In 1982, Bob Haro created the world's first freestyle specific frame, aptly named the Haro Freestyler. 40 years later, we pay homage to its iconic twin top tube design and timeless aesthetic. The Haro 26\" Freestyler is updated with a highly polished aluminum frame, matched with 4-piece chromoly bars and forks, all with the original Haro livery. The rest of the bike is built up with our very own Legends CNC-machined sprocket, Fusion pedals, and Bob's original artwork on the saddle and the included pad set. If you're a fan of Bob, Haro Bikes (or both), this is the bike for you.\n6061-T6 heat treated alloy frame w/integrated head tube, mid BB shell & disc brake\n1 1/8\" threadless full chromoly fork w/internally threaded steerer tube & tapered legs\nHaro Baseline 3-piece crhomoly 8 Spline 175mm\nHaro Retro alloy, chromoly 9/16\" axle pedals\nHaro Bob Bar\n36 hole double wall rims\nHaro Bob Seat\nHaro Lineage CNC Stem\nHaro Team Grips",
